{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>At the mouth of YHWH they journeyed.</b> We learned in the matter of the work of the Tabernacle: When Israel journeyed, the pillar of cloud would fold up and stretch out over the tribe of Judah like a beam. They would sound the teki'ah, the teru'ah, and the teki'ah — but it would not move until Moses said ״קוּמָה ה׳״ — this is in the Sifrei — and the standard of the camp of Judah would journey." "<b>And at the mouth of YHWH they encamped.</b> When Israel encamped, the pillar of cloud would tower upward and rise and spread out over the tribe of Judah like a booth. And it would not disperse until Moses said ״שׁוּבָה ה׳ רִבְבוֹת אַלְפֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״. Hence you say ״עַל פִּי ה׳ וּבְיַד מֹשֶׁה״ (baraita of the work of the Tabernacle, chapter 13)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:07.877068464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}